{"availability":"available","full":"Rizzo-AI-Academy/rizzo-flow","name":"rizzo-flow","description":"The open, local take on Jev: typed decisions from an LLM, without generating a single token","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":897,"forks":61,"created":"2026-09-21T00:00:02Z","updated":"2026-09-25T21:15:27Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://rizzo-ai-academy.github.io/rizzo-flow/","topics":[],"demo":"https://rizzo-ai-academy.github.io/rizzo-flow/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.145Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.145Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.145Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:21.220Z","stars":877,"forks":57},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.145Z","stars":897,"forks":61}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Unstructured state in → typed, probabilistic decisions out. On your own machine.","🌐 Website · A project by Rizzo AI Academy · 🇮🇹 Documentazione dettagliata in italiano","Rizzo Flow is an open-source, local-first implementation of the idea behind Jev, TypeSafe's \"System One\" model: a function call with judgment that takes unstructured state and returns typed decisions with probabilities — a yes/no, a choice among options, a score on a rubric, a number — instead of text you then have to parse."],"features":["Every question becomes a multiple choice. Each candidate answer is mapped to one uppercase","The state is processed once. It sits at the start of the prompt, so it is prefilled a","Only the answer letters are read. One position per question, the logits of the allowed","Plain Python turns logits into typed output. Softmax, optional temperature, expected values"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Rizzo-AI-Academy/rizzo-flow/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"45ed5fdfa5c7e32fbd99ad1c822896bf6c098a683bfaebe083c379a3c39c21f5","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:21.328Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.